# F030TieFighter — .gitignore
# Rule: the repo holds everything needed to re-run the analysis (docs, plans,
# scripts, sweeps, probes, the pristine 92 MB game copy). Bulk media that can
# be re-fetched/re-derived stays local.

# Source ROM (413 MB) — extract with 7-Zip into game/SWTieCD/TIECD (already in repo)
/Star Wars TIE Fighter (Collectors CD-ROM) (1995).zip

# CD image (595 MB, distribution only — the game runs from the TIECD folder)
game/SWTieCD/cd/

# Genuine MS-DOS 6.22 install floppies: the .7z at repo root is the source of
# truth; the extracted tree under img/ is derived
img/Microsoft MS-DOS 6.22*/

# QEMU disk images — all re-buildable, see analysis/qemu-boot.md.
# tie.hdd: 256 MB, `python work/build_dos_hdd.py`. Its .geom.json sidecar is tiny
# but derived, so it goes too. bootprep.img is committed (1.5 MB).
# tie-dos.img is the superseded superfloppy (the old `DIR C:` bug).
img/tie.hdd
img/tie.hdd.geom.json
img/tie-dos.img
img/tie-dos.img.bak

# Upstream extender source trees (kept for reference; their own .git is ignored,
# they are subtrees here — see work/README.md + analysis/extender-eval.md)
work/dos32a/.git/
work/dos32a/.gitattributes
work/dos32a/.gitignore
work/zrdx/.git/

# Transient observation output (serial sinks are no-ops in this QEMU build anyway)
img/serial*.log
img/qemu-exit.txt

# Stale duplicate extraction (superseded by game/SWTieCD — the reference copy;
# missing the EXEs, has a stray .exo file). Keep local, not in repo.
/SWTieCD/

# Python junk
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Image build scratch + headless run output (all regenerable)
work/img_build/
work/qemu_out/
work/dos_files/

# Ghidra project database (27 MB binary, fully regenerable — analysis/functions.md §7).
# The .raw object slices and *_seeds.txt next to it are small and kept, like the
# existing z_tie_32.raw/z_tie_16.raw precedent.
work/ghidra/TIE.gpr
work/ghidra/TIE.rep/

# P4.2 ratchet outputs (regenerate with work/ratchet16.py)
work/ratchet/
work/ratchet32/
work/build/

# bulk decompile corpus (4.9 MB, regenerate per work/README.md)
work/ghidra_export/obj1_c.c

# Scratch captures and debug dumps that the emulator and capture helpers
# drop beside the sources. Anchored at the root: committed images live in
# subdirectories, which the leading / does not reach.
/*.png
/*.ppm
/hatari.out.txt
/hatari.err.txt
/*-dbg.txt

# Finder metadata, from the macOS side of the toolchain. Unanchored: these
# appear in whatever directory was browsed, not just the root.
.DS_Store
